# VlogOps — environment variable NAMES. No values live here, and none ever will.
#
# Real values live OUTSIDE this repository and are passed to the process by whoever runs
# it — `node --env-file=<path outside this repo>` is this estate's convention. Nothing in
# this repository opens that file, and nothing in this service reads a value from any file
# inside the repository.
#
# The service validates all of these at startup and refuses to run with a missing or
# malformed one, reporting every problem in a single error rather than the first.

# REQUIRED. The Postgres connection string for the Content Seed store. It is the ONLY
# database variable this service has, deliberately: a service with two ways to reach its
# store has two ways to reach the wrong one.
VLOGOPS_DB_URL=

# OPTIONAL. The repository Route 1 reads existing records from. Defaults to the repository
# this service lives in; set it only when intaking from a checkout elsewhere. This is a
# path, not a secret.
VLOGOPS_REPO_ROOT=

# ── Phase 3: Scribe's model seam ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are NOT validated at startup, deliberately. Phase 1 intake and Phase 2 compile must
# keep working on a machine that has never had a model configured, so the seam refuses at
# CALL time instead — loudly, by name, and never by substituting a different model.
#
# There is NO DEFAULT MODEL NAME. A configured gateway with no model named is also a
# refusal: this estate has already had a live 400 caused by defaulting to an alias the
# gateway did not register, and the ruling was that such a default must never survive
# preflight again. So both variables are required together, or Scribe declines to draft.

# The OpenAI-compatible gateway base URL, e.g. http://host:4000/v1
VLOGOPS_MODEL_GATEWAY_URL=

# OPTIONAL bearer credential for that gateway. Read straight from the environment into the
# request header and nowhere else — never logged, never returned, never stored on a package.
VLOGOPS_MODEL_GATEWAY_KEY=

# REQUIRED whenever VLOGOPS_MODEL_GATEWAY_URL is set. Name a model the gateway actually
# registers; this code will not guess what is on the other end of a URL.
VLOGOPS_SCRIBE_MODEL=
